    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Lab Meeting Bot\nthis is some notes you must configure \nTelegram scheduling assistant for the professor (Gemini agent + Google Sheets + Google Calendar/Meet)\n1. Credentials: Telegram bot token, Google Gemini API key, Google OAuth2 for Sheets and Calendar.\n2. In \"Is Professor Chat?\" replace YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID with your numeric chat id.\n3. In every Google Sheets tool pick the spreadsheet \"Lab Assistant\" (YOUR_SHEET_ID); tabs: Members (name|email|team|role), Meetings Log (timestamp|team|title|start|end|attendees|meet_link|status).\n4. In every Google Calendar tool pick the calendar (YOUR_CALENDAR_ID).\n5. Meet link = Additional Field \"Conference Data\" (solution Google Meet) in create_event_with_meet; invitation emails = \"Send Updates: all\". Verify the conference option in the node UI.\n6. Publish the workflow: Telegram Trigger only works when published, and one bot can have only one Telegram trigger.\n7. Settings > Error workflow: attach \"Lab Assistant - Error Alert\".\n\nThis Template made by Basmala Taha ",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "3f5045cb-0129-4af6-86d5-eb133617ce5b",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
